  "name": "PROTEIN - C",
  "code": "1575",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>1. Protein C is a vitamin K dependent protein that is present in Plasma as a Zymogen. Protein C is activated in vivo by thrombin in the&nbsp;presence of throbomodulin. Protein C can be activated in vitro by a protein traction drived from the venom of the copperhead snake&nbsp;agkistrodon contortrix controtrix.<br>2. Decreased levels of protein C are seen in Hereditary deficiencies or Acquired deficiency - due to liver disease, acute thrombosis, vitamin&nbsp;K deficiency, DIC, ARDS, postoperative states, etc. The common manifestations are superficial thrombophlebitis, deep vein&nbsp;thrombosis, and pulmonary embolism.</p>\n<p><strong>LIMITATIONS:</strong><br>Coumadin will lower protein C. Berichrome protein C detects the amidolytically active protein of the activated protein C, including the noncarboxylated molecules synthesized in vitamin K deficiency.</p>",
